I developed an Android software application using the MIT App Inventor visual programming environment. The source code is created by connecting and assembling multiple functional blocks, similar to a puzzle, depending on the requirements of each application.

The interface includes two sections:

- Designer: In this section, I created and edited the user interface. The editor includes a variety of visual components that can be arranged using drag and drop.
- Blocks: In this section, I implemented the application’s functionality by using and connecting logic blocks.

When the application is opened, the user is presented with the following interface. On this screen, the following elements can be observed:

- A label displaying the text: “Access Control System”;
- An “Administrative Access” button, which is used to navigate to screen 2;
- An “Stop Alarm” button, which turns off the buzzer/alarm when pressed;
- FirebaseDB1, which is responsible for sending data to Firebase and stopping the alarm.
